{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7784649","formula":"C₁₄H₂₃NO₂S","hill":"C14H23NO2S","elements":["H","C","N","O","S"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"H":23.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"Thiobuscaline"},"descriptions":{"en":"Thiobuscaline (TB), or 4-thiobuscaline (4-TB), also known as 3,5-dimethoxy-4-butylthiophenethylamine, is a psychoactive drug of the phenethylamine and scaline families related to the psychedelic drug mescaline. It is the analogue of buscaline in which the butoxy group at the 4 position has been replaced with a butylthio group. The drug is a non-hallucinogenic serotonin 5-HT2A receptor agonist with similar effects and potential uses to those of Ariadne."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":44349865,"mass":269.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCSC1=C(C=C(C=C1OC)CCN)OC","inchikey":"CPNWMHCBHUXITO-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(4-butylsulfanyl-3,5-dimethoxyphenyl)ethanamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"44349865","atoms":41,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.062,"y":-1.017,"z":0.572,"el":"S"},{"x":-0.247,"y":-2.83,"z":-0.185,"el":"O"},{"x":0.81,"y":1.701,"z":1.071,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.588,"y":1.328,"z":-1.348,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.365,"y":0.107,"z":0.25,"el":"C"},{"x":4.109,"y":-0.264,"z":-1.174,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.808,"y":0.472,"z":0.145,"el":"C"},{"x":0.332,"y":-0.577,"z":0.446,"el":"C"},{"x":2.64,"y":-0.684,"z":-1.118,"el":"C"},{"x":4.406,"y":1.036,"z":-0.421,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.607,"y":-1.542,"z":0.082,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.077,"y":0.73,"z":0.712,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.956,"y":-1.2,"z":-0.016,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.426,"y":1.072,"z":0.614,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.181,"y":0.95,"z":-1.265,"el":"C"},{"x":5.858,"y":1.456,"z":-0.596,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.242,"y":-3.74,"z":0.911,"el":"C"},{"x":0.28,"y":3.001,"z":1.319,"el":"C"},{"x":4.741,"y":-1.071,"z":-0.783,"el":"H"},{"x":4.386,"y":-0.137,